    "field": "Climate change impacts on the cryosphere",
    "problem": "Assessments of future permafrost extent under climate change are unavailable for the Southern Hemisphere, preventing informed decision-making for water supply and climate adaptation strategies in arid mountain regions where glaciers are receding and alternative water sources are increasingly important.",
    "method": "This study uses downscaled climate model outputs and the 0\u00b0C mean annual air temperature as a proxy to calculate projected changes in permafrost extent and estimate the future activity of existing rock glaciers in the Bolivian Andes under 21st-century warming.",
    "task": "The task is to project the impact of future climate warming on permafrost extent and rock glacier activity in the Bolivian Andes by using downscaled climate model outputs and temperature thresholds as proxies for permafrost suitability.",
